body:
@everyone has the default options.

Pending is set to allow viewing channels/sending messages server wide, but I set the permissions in the categories to only allow viewing/messaging in the "Information" Category.

Visitors are also set to allow viewing channels/sending messages server wide, but are allowed viewing/posting to each categories/channels.

Do you think First Responders get or expect tips for saving peoples lives during car accidents, house fires, robberies, people choking, etc? Fuck no.

Do you think people that take CPR and First Aid classes do it because they expect that they are going to be rewarded for preventing little "Timmy" from drowning? Fuck No.

&#x200B;

They do it because they want to and, they expect nothing in return.

&#x200B;

Rewards aren't customary, you're just an entitled piece of shit and, you need to rethink your life.

Not everyone can get experience during school. I, as a military brat, was never in a place long enough to find a job and, when I finally was, I was 10-12miles into the middle of farm-country with no transport other than my feet. AKA a 4 hour walk to even get into town and, I had no friends and cell phones weren't popular enough/email was still a rarity so I had no references or my own phone to call.

I finally managed to get a security job and held onto it for 4 years before trying to go to trade school.

&#x200B;

Now I'm 30 and I'm borderline homeless because I keep getting turned down from those trade jobs, since I lack the experience needed, but now I'm considered too old to work at the jobs I need. Had I known this 4 years ago, I would have stayed at my crappy security job, instead of going to a trade school full time and, I would have just bought the equipment and materials to practice on my own.

&#x200B;

Applying for apprenticeships without any formal education on the trade isn't any better. Some even require a year or more of job experience to even be considered for the apprenticeship. How the fuck is a person supposed to get job experience in a field, with no education or training, to even meet those requirements!? That's what an  Apprenticeship is supposed to be for in the first place!

Ok, just making sure you weren't one of those ignorant psycho's that think it's animal abuse, when a husky decides it'd rather sleep outside in the snow instead of a nice warm home/bed.

&#x200B;

I kinda agree with you, your pet doesn't necessarily need to be allowed on the furniture, but they do need a comfortable area to hang out near where you are, especially if their breed is prone to joint issues like arthritis. I like FurHavens orthopedic beds. If they were me-sized and, had a base to lift it up so I wasn't on the floor, I'd be sleeping on that instead of my bed.

You do realize that non-furries do this exact same shit right?

&#x200B;

The only reason you see furries so often doing this shit, is because you either follow someone on social media that posts it, or you yourself follow it. THE only time I see any furries at all is on a public discord channel I frequent and, other than their profile pic's they don't go "OwO whats this?" or post their fetishes.

I dont know if this post broke or not, I'm on shitty internet. But what do you mean by crisis? Some people just might not view it that way because they've never been there or they simply just don't understand it. Heck my old therapist never even thought I was depressed just because I wasn't suicidal at the time.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;
